/-!
# The natural and dual recognition layers of G.2.5

The frame-root argument proves full I-invariance of S₃. Both literal
quotients are elementary abelian and carry canonical conjugation actions
through the specified starred comparison. The constructed natural and dual
point maps satisfy every G.1.3 clause. Applying that universal earlier
theorem gives the two homogeneous models, both printed marked direct sums,
and the actual coordinates used for counting and restriction to L₁.

The same construction is applied to the original binary flag of Section
12.8, including its series-collapse consumer. Multiplicity zero is retained.
The earlier G.2.2 and G.2.5(1–3) structural premises remain with
`qt-g02-linear-three`; the universally quantified G.1.3 implication remains
with `qt-g-01` through the G.2 assembly. No full source G.2.5 theorem is
claimed before those inputs are discharged.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
G.2.5, printed pp.335–336, PDF pp.346–347.
-/
